# MATTER_CAM_PATH for the M1d fly-through determinism gate on a STREAMED world.
# World: PomProofBrick -- three domes over streamed terrain sectors.
#
# The eye DESCENDS on a geometric ramp 420 m -> 6 m over a fixed ground point
# and never moves in x/z. Both properties are load-bearing:
#
#   fixed x/z  SectorStreamer measures sector distance in the horizontal plane
#              only (sector_streamer.cpp dist_to / desired_lod_for_dist), so a
#              purely vertical path leaves sector RESIDENCY untouched while the
#              renderer'''s 3D distance walks every resident sector down its rung
#              ladder. Residency churn would add publish-order noise on top of
#              the selection signal this gate is for.
#
#   descending the widest view is pose 0, so MATTER_CAM_PATH_WARMUP settles
#              every cluster the path will ever draw BEFORE the first compared
#              frame. Flown the other way (6 m -> 420 m) the same 48 sectors
#              are the same 48 sectors, but each one first enters the frustum
#              mid-path, and the rung it is first drawn at then races with
#              whatever fills its LOD records -- three sectors flipped between
#              rung 0 and rung 2 across four warm runs. That is a real engine
#              nondeterminism and worth its own gate; it is not what this path
#              is measuring.
#
# Run it with MATTER_CAM_PATH_WARMUP=300 (the 30-frame default does not settle
# a streamed world) and one pose per RENDERED frame:
#     eye_x eye_y eye_z target_x target_y target_z
